1
00:00:04,013 --> 00:00:06,343
(Leonard:)Hey, ready for lunch?
Oh, one sec.

2
00:00:06,349 --> 00:00:09,789
(Sheldon:)Is that the prototype drive
system for the high-G rover?

3
00:00:09,786 --> 00:00:12,156
(Howard:)No, Bernadette
got me a Fitbit

4
00:00:12,155 --> 00:00:15,195
(Howard:)so she can track
how much I'm exercising.

5
00:00:16,525 --> 00:00:19,795
(Leonard:)That'll teach her to care
about your health.

6
00:00:19,796 --> 00:00:23,566
(Howard:)I can't wait to see the look
on her face when I die young.

7
00:00:24,667 --> 00:00:26,067
(Raj:)When was the last actual
exercise you got?

8
00:00:26,069 --> 00:00:27,439
(Howard:)The other day, when

9
00:00:27,437 --> 00:00:30,877
(Howard:)she tried to put that Fitbit
on me and I ran away from her.

10
00:00:31,740 --> 00:00:33,340
(Sheldon:)According to a recent study,

11
00:00:33,343 --> 00:00:36,113
(Sheldon:)simply thinking about exercise,
even while sitting still,

12
00:00:36,112 --> 00:00:37,482
(Sheldon:)can have physical benefits.

13
00:00:37,480 --> 00:00:40,080
(Sheldon:)For all you know,
I could be exercising right now.

14
00:00:40,083 --> 00:00:42,983
(Raj:)Are you?
Eh, I'll do it tomorrow.

15
00:00:43,886 --> 00:00:45,186
(Leonard:)It wouldn't be the worst thing

16
00:00:45,188 --> 00:00:46,358
(Leonard:)if we were more active.

17
00:00:46,356 --> 00:00:48,756
Oh. You make
an excellent point.

18
00:00:51,927 --> 00:00:54,627
(Howard:)Ooh, I think
I'm getting a runner's high!

19
00:00:54,631 --> 00:00:58,271
♪ Our whole universe
was in hot, dense state ♪

